Morning Olu, Tom,

Thanks for the photos and the lot number, that confirms it. And the wobble you saw is real, it's not your eyes.

Return idlers from production lot 23-11 have an off-centre bore. It was a machining problem at our roller supplier. We =
caught it in early 2025, but by then the lot had gone out on new machines and as spares. The roller runs very slightly =
eccentric, which is enough to steer the return side of the belt. On a belt that's been running a while you often don't =
see it, because the old belt has taken a set and its edges have worn in. Put a new belt on and it follows the idler. Th=
e belt walks to the drive side every time, which is exactly what you've got.

The fix is to replace that return idler with the revised part, 77-0419. Same roller, corrected bore, and it has a blue =
end cap instead of black so you can tell them apart on the frame. It isn't in the parts list of your Rev B manual. Quot=
e 77-0419 to the distributor and they'll find it, or I can ship from Leeds. I'll send two at no charge, one for 0201 an=
d one for 0202 (see below). Please send me a delivery address in Fresno.

Until the idler arrives, this will let them run at full speed:

1. Set both take-up screws back to equal, at the position that gives you the 0.4% you measured. Your tension was right,=
 don't change it.
2. Shim the tail pulley bearing on the drive side by 0.5 mm. The shim goes behind the bearing block, between the block =
and the take-up slide, so the drive-side end of the tail pulley moves 0.5 mm back towards the tail. Use one 0.5 mm piec=
e of stainless shim, not a stack of thin ones.
3. Run the belt and re-check the tracking after three belt revolutions. On that length at line speed that's a couple of=
 minutes. It should settle and hold centre. If it's still walking after three revolutions, stop and ring me, because th=
en it's something else.
4. When you fit the 77-0419, take the shim out again, set the take-up even, and re-check after three revolutions as bef=
ore.

This affects BX-12 built in 2023 and 2024. Your 0202 (BX12-240078) came off the line the same week as 0201 and very lik=
ely has a 23-11 idler as well. It will show itself the day you change that belt, so I'd swap the idler at its next PM r=
ather than wait. If you have BX-20s anywhere, they use a different idler and aren't affected.

Sorry this has cost you and the plant a week. We should have put a bulletin out on it, and we haven't. I've raised that=
 again internally this morning.

Kind regards,
Henrik

