The lot stamp on the return idler nearest the tail reads 23-11. It was faint, Tom had to clean it with brake cleaner be=
fore we could read it. The label on the other end says 77-0410.

Belt edge at the tail is about 15 mm left of where it starts after 20 minutes, then it reaches the sensor. That's photo=
 3.

Take-up: we don't have a record of where the screws were before the change. Tom thinks they were close to even, near th=
e factory marks. Before your email the left screw was about four turns further in than the right. Yes, I know.

One thing I didn't mention before. With the belt slack, if you spin that idler by hand it doesn't look perfectly true t=
o me, there's a slight wobble you can see against the frame member behind it. Could be my eyes. The other return idlers=
