Hi Olu,

Email is fine, the ticket and I will catch up with each other.

Thanks for the detail, that saves us a round. Before I say anything that sends you down the wrong road, could you send =
me:

1. A photo of the return idler nearest the tail, the one under the frame roughly 600 mm in from the tail pulley. One fr=
om the side and one looking along the roller.
2. The lot number stamped on the roller end. It's on the end face of the roller tube, at the opposite end to the part n=
umber label. Four digits with a dash. You'll want a torch and probably a rag, they're not easy to read once there's bee=
n some washdown on them.
3. A photo of the belt edge at the tail pulley with the belt running, so I can see how far over it has gone.
4. If you know it, roughly how far you've moved each take-up screw from where it was before the belt change.

And please don't adjust the take-up any further for now. Four rounds of adjustment that keep coming back usually means =
you're correcting something that isn't at the tail, and the more you skew the tail pulley the harder the new belt edge =
works against the side guide.

I'm on a customer site in Coventry on Monday morning but will have the laptop with me.

Kind regards,
Henrik

