Hi Henrik,

Belton support in Leeds gave me your name and said you're the FAE who covers the BX range for North American customers.=
 They've logged it on their side too, but said email would get to you faster. Apologies if it should have gone through =
the ticket.

We service a BX-12 at Sierra Springs Beverage in Fresno, California: asset FRS-V-0201, serial BX12-240077, commissioned=
 March 2024. It's the case conveyor feeding the shrink wrapper on line 2. On Wednesday (May 6) Tom Becker and I replace=
d the belt. The old one had a torn edge next to the splice. The new belt is your 77-1012, 600 mm PU food grade, bought =
through your US distributor, fitted per the belt replacement section of the Rev B manual, direction of travel checked a=
gainst the arrow on the belt.

Since then the belt runs left. Looking downstream toward the wrapper, left is the motor side. It isn't dramatic at firs=
t. Over 20 to 30 minutes it creeps over until the edge sensor trips C-02 and the line stops. Yesterday they had seven C=
-02 stops on one shift, and the plant noticed.

What we've done so far:
- Tracking adjustment per the manual, on the tail take-up. I've adjusted it four times now. Each time it runs centred f=
or a while and then drifts back left. The two take-up screws are now a long way from even, which can't be right.
- Belt tension checked with the elongation method, marks 1,000 mm apart: 0.4%, which is inside the range in the manual.=
 I didn't want to go tighter.
- Frame checked for square, diagonals within 2 mm of each other.
- Drive and tail pulleys clean, no product build-up, lagging on the drive pulley is fine.
- The sister conveyor next to it, FRS-V-0202 (BX12-240078), still has its original belt and tracks fine.

The old belt ran centred for two years on this frame, so I don't think the frame has moved. Is there anything known abo=
ut new belts on the BX-12? I'd rather not keep cranking the take-up. The customer wants it right before their Monday ru=
n, they have a promotional pack going through next week.

Our reference is Corvane case 00041750 if you need one.

Thanks,
Olu

